{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "2TI",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I charge ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the sight of God, and of Christ Jesus, who shall judge the living and the dead, and by his appearing and his kingdom:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "preach the word; be urgent in season, out of season; reprove, rebuke, exhort, with all longsuffering and teaching.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the time will come when they will not endure the sound doctrine; but, having itching ears, will heap to themselves teachers after their own lusts;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "and will turn away their ears from the truth, and turn aside unto fables.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But be thou sober in all things, suffer hardship, do the work of an evangelist, fulfil thy ministry.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I am already being offered, and the time of my departure is come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have fought the good fight, I have finished the course, I have kept the faith:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "henceforth there is laid up for me the crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous judge, shall give to me at that day; and not to me only, but also to all them that have loved his appearing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Give diligence to come shortly unto me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "for Demas forsook me, having loved this present world, and went to Thessalonica; Crescens to Galatia, Titus to Dalmatia.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Only Luke is with me. Take Mark, and bring him with thee; for he is useful to me for ministering.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Tychicus I sent to Ephesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The cloak that I left at Troas with Carpus, bring when thou comest, and the books, especially the parchments.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Alexander the coppersmith did me much evil: the Lord will render to him according to his works:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "of whom do thou also beware; for he greatly withstood our words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At my first defence no one took my part, but all forsook me: may it not be laid to their account.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the Lord stood by me, and strengthened me; that through me the message might be fully proclaimed, and that all the Gentiles might hear: and I was delivered out of the mouth of the lion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Lord will deliver me from every evil work, and will save me unto his heavenly kingdom: to whom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the glory for ever and ever. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Salute Prisca and Aquila, and the house of Onesiphorus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Erastus remained at Corinth: but Trophimus I left at Miletus sick.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Give diligence to come before winter. Eubulus saluteth thee, and Pudens, and Linus, and Claudia, and all the brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2TI.4.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Lord be with thy spirit. Grace be with you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
